WEBVTT

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:19.240
"Together with Maman"

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.500
<i>Together with Maman</i>!

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.040
Hello, kids!

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.460
How are you?!

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.170
I'm Uramichi Oniisan! Gather around!

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:34.600
Yep, yep. I'm glad that everyone
joining me today is so energetic!

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.230
I wonder who's head-butting
the back of my knees.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:40.850
Hm?

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.730
Stop it right now, okay?!

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:47.360
Okay! Today's <i>Together</i>
<i>with Maman </i>is starting now!

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.610
You look kind of pale.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.320
Kids. Be very careful
to avoid the one-two punch

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.200
of having a hang over and
not enough sleep, okay?

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:28.580
"Life Lessons with Uramichi Oniisan"

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:34.670
Episode 5: Once This Concert Is Over...

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.670
"Before the start"           "Start shooting"
"Standby"                "Sign comes down"

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.940
Uramichi Oniisan. The next shoot will
start soon, so please standby.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:46.980
Okay!

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.150
Hello, kids!

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.860
How are you?! I'm Uramichi Oniisan!

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.820
Cut! Cut!

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:02.580
How you enter is always the same.
I've gotten tired of it.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:06.370
Hmm... Let's see...

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.500
Ah!

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:11.750
Wouldn't it be more interesting if you
appear while doing things like backflips?

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:15.300
I don't think... there is... enough space.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.930
Oh, please try it! I wanna see it!

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:21.850
Okay.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.480
Hello!

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.740
I'm Uramichi Oniisan!

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:42.410
Well, the usual way may be better
after all. Let's go with the usual way.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:45.580
For you, Uramichi-<i>kun</i>,
the usual way really is the best.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.540
Right.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:56.220
Kids! Come gather around me!

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:59.050
Okay, okay! Cut! Cut!

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:03.260
On second thought,
you did the backflip only once.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:06.770
That might be why it felt unsatisfying.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:08.940
Let's see...

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:12.360
Hmm... What do you think about, you know,

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:17.860
calling out to the kids while you
continuously do backflips?

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.360
What do I think?

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:25.120
I'd like to teach them not to approach
someone who's doing unsafe things.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:28.790
I want you to do it! Don't hold back!

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.080
Very well.

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:57.740
Yeah? Hello?

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:01.990
What? You got the wrong number.
I'm not Tanaka. I'm Derekida.

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:03.570
Yeah, that's right. What?

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:06.660
Like I said, I'm Derekida, not Tanaka!

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.790
Jeez...

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:15.840
Well, sorry, sorry! It was a wrong number.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.300
So, what were we talking about?

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:22.930
Um...

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:25.220
Well...

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:30.230
You really are the best, Uramichi-<i>kun</i>!
Let's do our best today again!

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:35.310
Okay!

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:39.480
Unknown

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:39.400
Uramichi Oniisan.

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:42.860
Oh, he's doing something.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.450
What's he doing?

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:49.160
What are they making you do by yourself?

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:53.370
It's like the "paw" or "sit"
command for dogs.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.840
If I do this, I can live to see tomorrow.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:00.380
You can't live unless
you do things like that?

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:05.890
Right.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:07.390
Poor thing...

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:11.600
Do you live because you
wanna do things like that?

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:14.940
"This isn't what I want to do"...
Those are the words

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:20.860
people who don't have anything specific
that they want to do say the most.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:26.240
Okay! So, kids! Let's smooth things
over by faking cheerfulness!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.830
Today is the Uramichi riddle day
that you've all been waiting for!

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:33.790
I was up late alone in my apartment
coming up with this riddle,

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:35.460
so do your best to answer it, okay?!

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.580
Okay!

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:42.670
Here is the question. What are the things
you kids have, but adults don't?

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:43.720
Kindergarten!

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:44.880
New Year's money gift!

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.220
Tricycle!

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:47.850
Nap time!

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:49.510
Drawing time!

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:51.560
Presents from Santa!

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:53.810
Yep, yep. That's great!

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:56.100
You've got all correct
answers up to this point!

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.520
Keep the answers coming!

00:06:58.520 --> 00:06:59.690
Freedom.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.480
Heart.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:02.740
Hope.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:06.280
Correct answers.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:09.950
Uramichi Riddle Ideas
Riddle Collection

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:09.950
What adults don't have

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:09.950
Decided

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:09.870
Uramichi Oniisan.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:16.370
Okay, kids! Before the ABC Exercise,
let's call out to our jolly friends!

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:17.830
One, two...!

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:20.460
--Usa--
--Usao-<i>kun</i>!
--I'm right here!

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:24.380
You were so quick to come out
that it was almost unnatural.

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:27.260
Did you want to play with
the kids as soon as possible?

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:31.390
I know both of you like them so much!

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:33.350
I like them so much, <i>kuma</i>!

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:35.640
Not really, hop!

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:36.850
Huh?

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:37.810
Ah...!

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:40.110
No... it's not like that...

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:46.200
Th-They just played the pre-recorded
audio at the wrong time.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.450
No... Seriously...

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:51.830
You just staring at me... is scary.
No, I can't take it...

00:07:54.620 --> 00:08:00.000
Now, kids! Get into the rhythm!
Let's start the ABC Exercise!

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:14.100
Now, this is the last one.
Stretch your back!

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.680
That's right! You're doing good!

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:20.560
Next up is your favorite,
the Bunny Exercise!

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:27.150
If you can do a better job than Usao-<i>kun</i>,
he said he'd do something funny.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:28.530
What?!

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:30.160
--Yay!
--All right!

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:33.530
Usao-<i>kun</i>! What're you going to do for us?!

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:36.290
You just need to do better than them.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:34.910
Murmur...

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:37.910
Just do better.

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:49.050
All right, you did a good job!

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:51.680
You kids won!

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:57.770
Seriously...!

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:57.770
"Green Rooms for Cast"

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:58.510
"Green Room
for Uramichi Omota-<i>sama</i>"

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:58.730
Seriously...!

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:00.640
Uramichi-<i>san</i>!

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.820
What?

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:09.490
Ah... Well... Um...

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:14.370
I'd like you to stop using us <i>kohai</i>
as your stress release...

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:16.240
I mean, um...

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.620
I don't do that.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:22.250
And my stress isn't something that
can be released with that kind of stuff.

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:28.010
Uramichi-<i>san</i>.

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:30.920
If you're struggling with something...

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:33.260
...you can tell us about it if you'd like.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.340
Yeah.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.770
You know...

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:45.360
...worries turn into vague
anxieties before you know it.

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:48.650
--Ahh...
--Err...

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:57.120
Thank you for coming today!

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:58.990
See you next time!

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:00.330
Bye-bye!

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:01.870
See you next time!

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:04.000
Excuse me, may I shake your hand?

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:04.450
Sure!

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:06.380
Thank you very much!

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:09.590
Goodbye! I hope to see you again!

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:11.010
Hm?

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:13.340
Uramichi Oniisan.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.390
What's up?

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:20.390
Um... Daddy's got a day off,

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:21.640
so...

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:22.890
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:27.020
I can go to see the concert next week!

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:28.980
I'm looking forward to it!

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:32.690
Yeah!

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:37.030
Thank you! We're looking forward
to seeing you there, too!

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:40.740
Bye-bye!

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.250
Bye-bye!

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:50.420
Come to think of it, the concert
is next week, isn't it?

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:52.970
I totally forgot about it.

00:10:55.970 --> 00:11:00.600
Every year, these concerts seem
to take more out of me.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:02.810
They put me in low spirits.

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:05.190
I have a coupon for a gym if you like.

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:09.060
But the gym you go to
is a full-scale one, right?

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:12.360
There's no way I'd join yours!

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:15.150
In any case, let's do our best.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:15.990
Yeah.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:24.410
"Together Concert"

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:29.250
Man... Working on a day
that is normally our day off...

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.630
I wanna go out on a date.

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:34.670
But you don't have a girlfriend.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:36.380
Yeah, I have to resolve that first.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:40.180
The concert starts in less than an hour!

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:43.020
Change your clothes soon
and get ready, okay?!

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:44.770
You guys, too!

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:48.310
Now, straighten up!

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:49.900
Jeez...

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:54.780
Ah... What a busy day.

00:11:56.240 --> 00:12:00.740
That choreographer only gets
fired up when we have a concert.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:06.040
He's strangely aspirational and keeps
running rehearsals on the concert day.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:14.300
But because of that, they're almost
dead by the time the concert starts.

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:19.180
Once this concert is over,
I'll take a paid leave.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:23.720
Get real. We don't have
paid leave to start with.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:28.230
Once this concert is over,
I'll get married.

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:31.810
Seriously, be careful what
you say. You might jinx it.

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:40.320
Hello, kids!

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:45.910
Welcome to the Together Concert!

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:48.460
I'm Usao-<i>kun</i>, hop!

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:51.290
I'm Kumao-<i>kun</i>, <i>kuma</i>!

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:55.670
We're so happy to see you all!

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:59.720
Let's play together a lot today!

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:06.350
Hello!

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:10.350
I'm Iketeru Daga, your singer Oniisan!

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.350
Hello!

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:15.900
I'm Utano Tadano, your singer Oneesan!

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:19.860
Thank you for coming to see us today!

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:24.030
Hey, hey, Iketeru Oniisan.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:27.160
What are some things you're good at?

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:28.700
Hmm...

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:31.750
I guess I'd have to say singing.

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:36.040
But also, you're not good
at reading analog watches, right?

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:37.800
Well, it's more like...

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:40.340
Er... Right...

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:44.180
Everyone has things that they're
good at and not so good at.

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:46.850
That's so wonderful, isn't it?

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:52.480
We're first going to sing this
cheerful song that's perfect for us!

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:55.150
"Can and Can't"!

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:55.180
Can and Can't

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:01.570
♬ Some things you can do,
and others you can't ♬

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:06.660
♬ Don't try to do everything yourself! ♬

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:09.910
♬ If someone can do something you can't ♬

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:15.420
♬ Say "Nice work!"
and become their friend ♬

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:21.220
♬ Some people are good singers ♬

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:24.550
♬ Some people know how to draw ♬

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:28.310
♬ Some people tell funny stories ♬

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:33.810
♬ And some are great jumpers ♬

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:42.400
♬ We're all just people--ordinary people ♬

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:48.620
♬ There's more things
you can't do than can ♬

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:55.670
♬ The things you can do
aren't the things you want to ♬

00:14:55.670 --> 00:14:58.670
♬ If someone can do what you can't ♬

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:02.550
♬ It's hard to be their friend ♬

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:06.090
♬ You can't get out the "Nice work!" ♬

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:12.770
♬ Saying "Nice work!"
and becoming friends ♬

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:19.360
♬ That's the hardest thing of all ♬

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:22.110
Thank you, everyone!

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:34.080
Hello, kids! I'm Uramichi Omota,
your gymnast Oniisan!

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:36.040
How are you?!

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:39.000
Hello!

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.380
Usao-<i>kun </i>is here, too, hop!

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:44.670
Kumao-<i>kun </i>is also here, kuma!

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:48.340
I'm good at jumping and tumbling!

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:51.680
But no matter how many times
you jump or tumble,

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:56.190
there are ideas and gloomy thoughts
that you can't shake off, right?

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:59.860
Someone said to me,
"You're not kind" in the past,

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:03.480
and it still remains in my heart.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:08.530
It's probably the case that
I'm not good at being nice to others.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:09.820
But...!

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:19.370
...if kindness means sticking
your nose in others' business,

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:24.340
I don't think you kids need to try
too hard to become a kind person!

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.840
Next up is this song!

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:32.840
The Cat's Staring at Nothing Again

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:32.840
Performed by: Utano Oneesan

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:32.760
"The Cat's Staring at Nothing Again"!

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:38.390
♬ What are you looking at?
What is it you see over there? ♬

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:42.480
♬ There's nothing there at all (nothing) ♬

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:45.690
♬ I don't have any furniture ♬

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:49.240
♬ Or money, or time ♬

00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:52.990
♬ Or food in the fridge ♬

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:57.700
♬ Only my cat ♬

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:03.630
♬ He isn't any use at all,
but at least he's here ♬

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:08.010
♬ That's enough for me ♬

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:13.220
♬ So tell me--what are you looking at? ♬

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:17.100
♬ Nothing! There's nothing! ♬

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:17.090
"Fish Dealer"

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:20.940
♬ My life is all for nothing ♬

00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:26.020
♬ I'm still alive, though I have nothing ♬

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:45.290
Everyone! Thank you for coming today!

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:49.800
Let's play again!

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:51.630
Bye-bye!

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:53.470
Bye-bye!

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:01.980
Ahh... We finished it.

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:03.650
Good work.

00:18:03.650 --> 00:18:05.230
Good work.

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:06.320
You guys!

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:07.190
Hm?

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:10.740
It was wonderful! Well done!

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:11.610
Thank you.

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:12.860
This is your reward.

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:14.160
Well... Ah...

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:22.160
Hey, guys! Good work, good work.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:26.250
Well, it was indeed a good concert...

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:29.550
...though I wasn't paying
too much attention.

00:18:29.550 --> 00:18:31.380
Yeah...

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:34.930
Okay, then, guys! You're going
to the after-party, right?

00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:36.390
I'm coming!

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:38.510
Beer! Beer!

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:41.270
Oh? Where's Uramichi Oniisan?

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:42.980
He's already gone home.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:00.070
Refreshing feelings race around

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:01.950
Cheers!

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:24.850
<i>If I fall because I'm walking while only</i>
<i>looking up, I'd rather be looking down</i>

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:29.400
<i>There are things you can only notice</i>
<i>when you're looking down</i>

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:29.900
<i>See? There's a small crab over there</i>
<i>  </i>

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:31.570
